course: dictionary
lesson: 9547
title: Stop and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word stop has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» Here stops means she no longer shares secrets, so stop means to end an action or to not do something any more.
explain: Stop can also be a noun, a thing or place. «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now» uses the verb. A bus stop is a place where a bus waits for people. Ask yourself: is this word doing an action, or naming a place or thing?
explain: Stop can be casual or formal. «Stop it!» is a blunt order, but «Stop!» after a joke can mean «that's so funny». In a formal text, «cease» or «halt» may be used instead. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Stop is a verb (stop, stops, stopped, stopping) and also a noun.
fact: «Stops» in «Ruby stops games an hour before bed» means ends or no longer does something.
fact: A full stop (UK) is the dot at the end of a sentence. In the US it is called a period.
fact: A bus stop or train stop is where people wait to get on and off.
fact: «Stop by» or «stop over» means visit briefly, and «cease», «halt» and «terminate» are stiff, formal words for stop.
exercise: «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» What does stops mean here? | Tells everyone the secrets | *Ends the habit of sharing | Shouts loudly at her friend | Walks quickly to the door
exercise: Mia waits at the bus stop every morning. What is a bus stop? | A long holiday from school | A dot at the end of a sentence | *A place where a bus waits for people | A kind of bread
exercise: «The loop stops, and n is 21.» What does stops mean? | Gets louder | *Comes to an end | Goes faster and faster | Starts again from zero
test: Your friend says «Stop!» after a very funny joke. What does this casual slang mean? | Take a break from school | Please stop walking now | Go away and leave me alone | *That's so funny
test: Which word is a formal word that means stop? | *Cease | Stop it | Full stop | Stop by
exam: In British English, what is a full stop? | A short break in a trip | Another word for go on | *The dot at the end of a sentence | Any stop on a bus route
